From ddf5d0a9d9e24d4cc4e2b6b30f365fcacddc77dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Milad <mmaziesf@uwaterloo.ca>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:48:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] glasses.capture: frames straight from the iPhone app,
 pre-armed per turn

HOMEHUB_GLASSES_DISCOVER gets frames from the Glasses Bridge iPhone app
itself, so no PC relay is needed. The app serves GET /snapshot.jpg and
advertises _glasses-bridge._tcp; the gadget finds it with mDNS
(espressif/mdns: PTR, then an A query when the answer carries only the
SRV record), as soon as Wi-Fi is up, then every 30 s until found, and
again whenever the phone stops answering. mDNS runs only during a lookup
and is freed after it (its task and buffers are internal RAM the display
needs). HOMEHUB_GLASSES_CAPTURE_URL becomes the fallback; leave it empty
to use the phone only.

Pre-armed capture: each voice turn (wake word, tap) starts a background
fetch, so when Muse calls glasses.capture a few seconds later the frame of
the moment the user asked is already in memory. A capture waits up to 3 s
for a fetch in flight, uses a frame under 20 s old once, and otherwise
fetches live.
---
